  {
    "id": "p-ff1f8e",
    "offset": 16295,
    "text": "*Answers to § 9.* AN9"
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d7887b",
    "offset": 16318,
    "text": "1. Babies cannot manage crocodiles."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-8a7df6",
    "offset": 16355,
    "text": "2. *Your* presents to me are not made of tin."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7d6243",
    "offset": 16402,
    "text": "3. All my potatoes in this dish are old ones."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-a4d488",
    "offset": 16449,
    "text": "4. My servants never say \"shpoonj.\""
  },
  {
    "id": "p-0e38d5",
    "offset": 16486,
    "text": "5. My poultry are not officers."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-76d798",
    "offset": 16519,
    "text": "6. None of *your* sons are fit to serve on a jury."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-66ba1e",
    "offset": 16571,
    "text": "7. No pencils of mine are sugar-plums."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-f66045",
    "offset": 16611,
    "text": "8. Jenkins is inexperienced."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-749fc8",
    "offset": 16641,
    "text": "9. No comet has a curly tail."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-f07428",
    "offset": 16672,
    "text": "10. No hedge-hog takes in the *Times*."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-707572",
    "offset": 16712,
    "text": "11. This dish is unwholesome."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-8e0bf4",
    "offset": 16743,
    "text": "12. My gardener is very old."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-b07b05",
    "offset": 16773,
    "text": "13. All humming-birds are small."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-6781c8",
    "offset": 16807,
    "text": "14. No one with a hooked nose ever fails to make money."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-bd4557",
    "offset": 16864,
    "text": "15. No gray ducks in this village wear lace collars."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-7b7a73",
    "offset": 16918,
    "text": "16. No jug in this cupboard will hold water."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-82e245",
    "offset": 16964,
    "text": "17. These apples were grown in the sun."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-8477b8",
    "offset": 17005,
    "text": "18. Puppies, that will not lie still, never care to do worsted work."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c503a2",
    "offset": 17075,
    "text": "19. No name in this list is unmelodious."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-13ba8a",
    "offset": 17117,
    "text": "20. No M.P. should ride in a donkey-race, unless he has perfect self-command."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-74e02b",
    "offset": 17196,
    "text": "21. No goods in this shop, that are still on sale, may be carried away. pg133 22. No acrobatic feat, which involves turning a quadruple somersault, is ever attempted in a circus."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-230e2e",
    "offset": 17376,
    "text": "23. Guinea-pigs never really appreciate Beethoven."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e67737",
    "offset": 17428,
    "text": "24. No scentless flowers please me."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-617ec4",
    "offset": 17465,
    "text": "25. Showy talkers are not really well-informed."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c210b2",
    "offset": 17514,
    "text": "26. None but red-haired boys learn Greek in this school."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-deb465",
    "offset": 17572,
    "text": "27. Wedding-cake always disagrees with me."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-3b9ab5",
    "offset": 17616,
    "text": "28. Discussions, that go on while Tomkins is in the chair, endanger the peacefulness of our Debating-Club."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-b807a1",
    "offset": 17724,
    "text": "29. All gluttons, who are children of mine, are unhealthy."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-348be1",
    "offset": 17784,
    "text": "30. An egg of the Great Auk is not to be had for a song."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-3b9837",
    "offset": 17842,
    "text": "31. No books sold here have gilt edges, unless they are priced at 5s. and upwards."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-f0a8e0",
    "offset": 17926,
    "text": "32. When you cut your finger, you will find Tincture of Calendula useful."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-003614",
    "offset": 18001,
    "text": "33. *I* have never come across a mermaid at sea."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-da3dec",
    "offset": 18051,
    "text": "34. All the romances in this library are well-written."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e1b8ec",
    "offset": 18107,
    "text": "35. No bird in this aviary lives on mince-pies."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d83336",
    "offset": 18156,
    "text": "36. No plum-pudding, that has not been boiled in a cloth, can be distinguished from soup."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-ee66f7",
    "offset": 18247,
    "text": "37. All *your* poems are uninteresting."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-84b655",
    "offset": 18288,
    "text": "38. None of my peaches have been grown in a hot-house."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-044945",
    "offset": 18344,
    "text": "39. No pawnbroker is dishonest."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-8550ec",
    "offset": 18377,
    "text": "40. No kitten with green eyes will play with a gorilla."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-0e05c3",
    "offset": 18434,
    "text": "41. All *my* friends dine at the lower table."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-b1d0d7",
    "offset": 18481,
    "text": "42. My writing-desk is full of live scorpions."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-040518",
    "offset": 18529,
    "text": "43. No Mandarin ever reads Hogg's poems."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d272cb",
    "offset": 18571,
    "text": "44. Shakespeare was clever."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-383245",
    "offset": 18600,
    "text": "45. Rainbows are not worth writing odes to."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-792bfe",
    "offset": 18645,
    "text": "46. These Sorites-examples are difficult."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-021861",
    "offset": 18688,
    "text": "47. All my dreams come true."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-94b4b1",
    "offset": 18718,
    "text": "48. All the English pictures here are painted in oils."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-1fa9be",
    "offset": 18774,
    "text": "49. Donkeys are not easy to swallow."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-1e9817",
    "offset": 18812,
    "text": "50. Opium-eaters never wear white kid gloves."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e3fc74",
    "offset": 18859,
    "text": "51. A good husband always comes home for his tea."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-4c7096",
    "offset": 18910,
    "text": "52. Bathing-machines are never made of mother-of-pearl."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-062a49",
    "offset": 18967,
    "text": "53. Rainy days are always cloudy."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-d5d13e",
    "offset": 19002,
    "text": "54. No heavy fish is unkind to children."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-04c789",
    "offset": 19044,
    "text": "55. No engine-driver lives on barley-sugar."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-1dfc9d",
    "offset": 19089,
    "text": "56. All the animals in the yard gnaw bones."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-cc62e1",
    "offset": 19134,
    "text": "57. No badger can guess a conundrum."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-e2ccaa",
    "offset": 19172,
    "text": "58. No cheque of yours, received by me, is payable to order."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-255829",
    "offset": 19234,
    "text": "59. I cannot read any of Brown's letters."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-c797f2",
    "offset": 19277,
    "text": "60. I always avoid a kangaroo."
  },
  {
    "id": "p-35904d",
    "offset": 19309,
    "text": "pg134"
  }
]